{
  "description": "A family-aware diagnostic adapter for Self-EvolveRec that measures the behavior of each trained BERT4Rec model through the host ModelView interface and produces an interpretation prompt grounded in measured metrics and their definitions.",
  "motivation": "Make model revisions evidence-driven while preserving benchmark comparability, BERT4Rec semantics, dataset routing, and the requirement for one independently trained model per category.",
  "implementation_notes": "Retain DiagnosisProbe(view, device), run_full_diagnosis(train_loader), and diagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis). Return metrics and metric_definitions; explicitly mark unavailable measurements. Use view.model as the actual trained module and preserve item_emb, log2feats(sequence), and predict_score(features, items). Handle left padding using the final nonpadding position. Any predictive probe must respect masked-target training and appended-mask inference, without exposing targets in bidirectional inputs. Use only public histories, titles, descriptions, and timestamps; review content, ratings, commercial attributes, and simulator traits are unavailable. Generate full-catalog unseen-item recommendations for five real training users per category. Select revisions using macro validation HR@10 across all four categories, with fixed splits and seeds. Keep checkpoint loading and the embedded predictor consistent.",
  "pseudocode": "class DiagnosisProbe(view, device):\n    run_full_diagnosis(train_loader):\n        preserve model training state\n        switch view.model to evaluation mode\n        under no_grad:\n            inspect supported public-data availability\n            for (_, sequence, positive, negative) in train_loader:\n                compute family-compatible diagnostics\n                exclude padding and prevent target leakage\n                accumulate measured values and valid counts\n        restore model training state\n        return {metrics: aggregated measurements, metric_definitions: definitions and availability}\n\ndiagnosis_interpreter_prompt(raw_diagnosis):\n    include measured metrics, definitions, and missing-data limitations\n    request evidence-grounded interpretations and single-model BERT4Rec revisions\n    prohibit invented observations and test-based selection",
  "originality": {
    "score": 4,
    "positive": "Connects architecture-aware diagnostics with a constrained iterative recommendation workflow.",
    "negative": "The description specifies an adapter contract rather than a new diagnostic algorithm or learning method."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Could support reproducible diagnosis and targeted revisions as the BERT4Rec architecture evolves.",
    "negative": "Its practical value depends on choosing informative probes and demonstrating validation gains; no results are supplied."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "The fixed interfaces and batch shapes provide a clear integration boundary.",
    "negative": "Correct masking, padding, leakage prevention, metric aggregation, and predictor consistency require careful implementation."
  }
}
